    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the lineup, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.84). **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and the high-leverage leadoff spot against Warren. While his opponent's xERA is respectable, the park dimensions and his ability to contribute across all five categories\u2014particularly his aggressive base-running profile\u2014make him an elite anchor. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** carries a high floor into his matchup against Houser, whose 4.58 xERA suggests a prime environment for **Kyle Tucker** to drive in runs from the cleanup spot, maintaining an efficiency score that comfortably clears the \"Strong\" threshold.\n\nTactical edge-seeking remains our priority, particularly concerning stolen bases. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (72.45) highlight our focus on speed-first assets; both benefit from dynamic platoon advantages against right-handed starters, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically positioned to exploit Singer\u2019s tendencies. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.92) provides a high-ceiling anchor in the utility slot, even against a tough lefty like McClanahan, due to his consistent xwOBA metrics. The most difficult roster decision today involved **Josh Jung**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 55.03 efficiency score. Ultimately, **Josh Jung** was sidelined because the cumulative scoring projections for our primary infield and outfield starters, buoyed by superior platoon splits and superior lineup positioning, offered a higher aggregate expectation for our 5x5 categories.\n\nManagers should monitor **Nasim Nunez** and **Andy Pages** closely, as both carry slightly lower scores due to deeper lineup positioning. While **Josh Lowe** (62.89) is an aggressive start, we are factoring in a slight defensive discount against an elite catcher arm, though his potential for stolen bases keeps his floor secure. We are currently navigating no major weather threats, but the proximity of **Liam Hicks** (57.76) and **Nolan Schanuel** (55.93) to the \"Marginal\" threshold means we will be watching their early-game plate appearances closely; if the rhythm isn't there, we are prepared to shift to high-upside bench options like **Miguel Vargas** or **Coby Mayo** in future cycles.",
